'''thoria''' (thō′ri-ä̤), ''n.'' [NL., < ''Thor.''] An oxid of thorium, ThO<sub>2</sub>. {{smaller|When pure it is a white powder, without taste, smell, or alkaline reaction on litmus. Its specific gravity is 9.4. It is insoluble in all acids except sulphuric.}}

