4. In ''zoöl.'', some sharp process, horn, or spine. See ''spine'', 3.—5. In ''entom.'', one of certain geometrid moths: an English book-name. The little thorn is ''Epione advenaria;'' the early thorn is ''Selenia illunaria.''—6. In ''lace-making'', a small pointed projection used to decorate the cordon-net, etc. Compare ''spine'', 5.—7. The Anglo-Saxon letter þ, equivalent to ''th;'' also, the corresponding character in Icelandic.

{{smaller block|The English letter ''thorn'', þ, survived and continued in use down to the 15th century, when it was transformed to y.
